      "title": "Match loop review",
      "message": "After a full match, j is set to 0 for nonoverlap, but when the word-boundary check fails it sets j = prefix[j-1]. That is fine. However, if a needle has length 1 and the match is rejected, prefix[0] is 0 so it works. The real issue: in the KMP loop, `ch == needle[j]` is evaluated after j may equal len(needle)-1 only; fine. No bug here beyond this.",
